D; line-height: 1.5\">Found in his coat in the shed. Sent messages, Saturday.</div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex: 1; background: #ECE8E1; border: 6px solid #1E1B18; border-radius: 22px; padding: 14px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px; overflow: hidden\"><div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 4px; align-items: flex-end\"><div style=\"font-family: Inter, system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: 12px; color: #5C554D\">To: <b style=\"color: #1E1B18\">Anton</b> · 22:40</div><div style=\"max-width: 82%; background: #2F6FD6; color: #FFFFFF; border-radius: 14px 14px 4px 14px; padding: 9px 13px; font-family: Inter, system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.4\">I'm signing with the Swiss buyers on Monday – without you. Your shares are worth nothing. If you want to talk, I'll be in the shed.</div></div><div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 4px; align-items: flex-end\"><div style=\"font-family: Inter, system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: 12px; color: #5C554D\">To: <b style=\"color: #1E1B18\">Ingrid</b> · 22:41</div><div style=\"max-width: 82%; background: #2F6FD6; color: #FFFFFF; border-radius: 14px 14px 4px 14px; padding: 9px 13px; font-family: Inter, system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.4\">Sorry about earlier. Back soon.</div></div></div>\n</div></div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; gap: 24px; border-top: 2px solid #1E1B18; padding-top: 14px\">\n<div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px\">\n<div style=\"display: flex; gap: 8px\"><div style=\"width: 30px; height: 30px; border-radius: 50%; border: 2px solid #1E1B18; background: transparent; color: #1E1B18; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-family: Inter, system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700\">1</div><div style=\"width: 30px; height: 30px; border-radius: 50%; border: 2px solid #1E1B18; background: transparent; color: #1E1B18; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-family: Inter, system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700\">2</div><div style=\"width: 30px; height: 30px; border-radius: 50%; border: 2px solid #1E1B18; background: transparent; color: #1E1B18; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-family: Inter, system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700\">3</div><div style=\"width: 30px; height: 30px; border-radius: 50%; border: 2px solid #1E1B18; background: transparent; color: #1E1B18; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-family: Inter, system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700\">4</div><div style=\"width: 30px; height: 30px; border-radius: 50%; border: 2px solid #1E1B18; background: transparent; color: #1E1B18; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-family: Inter, system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700\">5</div><div style=\"width: 30px; height: 30px; border-radius: 50%; border: 2px solid #A4161A; background: #A4161A; color: #FFFFFF; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-family: Inter, system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700\">6</div></div>\n<div style=\"font-family: Inter, system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; color: #1E1B18\">Find all 6 clues, then scan the code to name the culprit.</div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 4px; width: 250px\">\n<div style=\"font-family: Inter, system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.12em; color: #5C554D\">NEXT CLUE IS HIDDEN …</div>\n<div style=\"border-bottom: 1.5px dashed #1E1B18; height: 30px\"></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>"}], "solution": {"killer": "Anton Berg", "motive": "Bernard was selling the chalet company to Swiss buyers without Anton, making Anton's shares worthless (clue 6).", "proof": ["The snow stopped at 23:10 (clue 2). The killer's tracks have no snow in them, so they were made after 23:10 (clue 1).", "The back door opened at 23:24 and 23:41 – there and back (clue 5). There is no door event at 22:30, so Anton's ‘firewood at half past ten’ story is false.", "The tracks have a ridged hiking-boot sole, and Anton's hiking boots were the only wet pair (clues 1 and 4).", "Bernard texted Anton at 22:40 to meet him in the shed (clue 6)."], "cleared": ["<b>Ingrid, Max, Pierre and Lena</b> were at the card table every round from 22:30 to 00:00 (clue 3).", "<b>Sven</b> came from the front, and the tracks only lead to and from the back door (clues 1 and 2)."]}}, {"slug": "the-gull-island-diamond", "level": 2, "crime": "Burglary", "who": "thief", "title": "The Gull Island Diamond", "teaser": "A priceless diamond vanishes from a safe on a tidal island. Only one road leads in – and the sea decides when.", "intro": "The <b>Gull Star</b> diamond has been stolen from Lady Eleanor Price's safe on Gull Island, which can only be reached by a causeway at low tide. Find all 6 clues, compare the statements and the evidence, and work out who did it.", "intro_text": "The Gull Star diamond has been stolen from Lady Eleanor Price's safe on Gull Island, which can only be reached by a causeway at low tide. Find all 6 clues, compare the statements and the evidence, and work out who did it.", "added": "", "daily": null, "public": "2026-11-14", "suspects": [{"name": "Lady Eleanor Price", "role": "Owner of Gull House"}, {"name": "Rosa Delgado", "role": "Housekeeper"}, {"name": "Callum Reid", "role": "Boatman and gardener"}, {"name": "Beatrice Lowe", "role": "Eleanor's niece"}, {"name": "Dr Simon Hart", "role": "Family doctor and guest"}, {"name": "Frederick Price", "role": "Eleanor's brother"}], "clues": [{"name": "Lady Eleanor Price", "role": "Owner of Gull House", "quote": "I wore the Gull Star at lunch and locked it in the library safe at half past seven, before dinner. At ten I opened the safe – empty. Whoever did it knew the combination.", "label":